  "tagline": "An incremental SQL engine grounded in DBSP theory that updates any SQL query from changes only.",
  "description": "Feldera grew out of VMware Research's DBSP work, which gives a mathematical framework for incrementally maintaining arbitrary SQL, including recursive queries and complex joins. You write pipelines as SQL tables and views; Feldera compiles them to Rust and processes inserts, updates and deletes so outputs change in proportion to input changes, not data size. It integrates with Kafka, Delta Lake, Iceberg, Postgres and HTTP. The core is MIT-licensed, with an enterprise edition and managed cloud from Feldera Inc. Releases ship several times per week.",
